[Music]  episode two of the second season of the  disney plus hit the mandalorian was as  egg-centric as anything in the star wars  universe and that includes plenty of  tasty hidden easter eggs for fans to  spot  here are a few you may not have caught  after returning from the successful  crate dragon hunt  the mandalorian returns to mos eisley  and chapter 10 the passenger  to meet with pelemato he reports back  and lets her know that the supposed  mandalorian frequenting mos  pelgo was just a man in mandalorian  armor but she reassures him that she can  put him in contact with someone who can  lead him to his people  first she introduces him to dr mandible  a giant bug-like creature whose brief  screen time carries with it a couple of  meanings  mandible appears to be a member of the  killik species  first introduced in the dark nest  trilogy of books by troy denning  a killik that may or may not be dr  mandible also appeared in episode 5 of  season 1 of the mandalorian  sitting at the cantina bar it's also  worth noting that filmmaker peyton reed  best known for the ant-man movies  directed the passenger  thus the inclusion of this ant inspired  character  seems a not so subtle nod to the  director's marvel cinematic universe  contributions  when mando first gets back to mos eisley  after a long  strenuous walk across the desert his  first stop is at the cantina where he  finds motto in the middle of a  high-stakes card game against  dr mandible the scene doesn't last long  and their game  isn't the focus by any means but the  cards in mato's hands point to one of  the star wars universe's favorite  pastimes  a good old fashioned game of sabac  sabacc is a staple of star wars  appearing in everything from books tv  shows video games  and obviously a few of the movies it's  mentioned now and again throughout the  skywalker saga  even popping up in the background of the  force awakens  but its most notable appearance came in  2018's  solo a star wars story in the film a  young lando calrissian  cheats a young han solo out of a game  but the smuggler later gets his future  ally back by using his techniques  against him to steal a win  walking away with a millennium falcon  turning back to the mandalorian here's a  neat detail  motto's unbeatable winning hand in the  passenger  is known as an idiot's array  and it's the same winning hand lando had  in a star wars rebels episode of the  same name  not so fast it appears i have an idiot's  array  just before departing for trask mando  and the child wait  inside peli mato's hangar for their  passenger to arrive  as a token of their appreciation they  leave her with a portion of the crate  dragon meat they secured in the previous  episode  which she cooks up rather peculiarly a  treadwell droid holds up the cut of meat  to the flames of a stationary podracer  engine to roast it  a reference to a real-life star wars  eatery located at disney's  galaxy's edge theme park the restaurant  in question  is ronto roasters a neat little place  with a menu  including something for everyone while  ronto roasters  doesn't have any crate dragon steaks for  sale one of its more decorative  elements draws a neat parallel to this  mandalorian scene  at the heart of the diner you can watch  droids cook  food beneath the pod racer engine in the  same fashion as motto's droid  even though it's all for show at the  amusement park it's nice to see this  method of food preparation makes its way  into  star wars canon proper mando in the  child's journey with their passenger the  frog lady and her container of eggs  becomes a bit complicated  since they can't utilize hyperspace  travel for the sake of her unborn  children  instead they have to make the journey to  the planet trask  at sublight meaning that anyone looking  for mando will have a much easier time  finding him  that includes the new republic's x-wing  patrols who pressed the bounty hunter  relentlessly for information about his  ship and his shady dealings  we're out here sweeping for imperial  holdouts one pilot in particular  likely stood out to seasoned star wars  fans from the moment he arrived on  screen  the mastermind behind both the clone  wars and star wars rebels and an  occasional mandalorian director  dave filoni makes a brief appearance in  the passenger in a reprisal of his  season one role as trapper wolf  the character made his franchise debut  in chapter 6 the prisoner  in which he alongside fellow directors  deborah chao  and rick famous destroys ransar malk's  space hangar  following the escape of new republic  prisoner quinn  following the crash landing in the razor  crest the mandalorian the child and the  frog lady are left to survive in the  bitter cold of an unnamed ice planet  fed up with mando's sluggishness and  repairing the ship  the frog lady wanders off into the snowy  labyrinth and finds a hot spring for  herself and her eggs  concerned for their safety mando tries  to get the frog lady and her precious  cargo out of the cave  and his hunch is right in a scene akin  to something from ridley scott's alien  or john carpenter's the thing the child  unintentionally awakens a den of  spider-like creatures  known as the krikna the krikna have a  long storied history in the star wars  universe  first realized in legendary concept  artist ralph mcquarrie's the empire  strikes back sketches and initially  known  as navi white spiders while they never  appeared in that film  the krikna eventually made their spine  tingling entrance during star wars  rebels second season  in the episode the mystery of chopper  bass they later appeared in a handful of  other installments of the series  but their introduction on the  mandalorian is their first in live  action  and for those with arachnophobia  hopefully their last  check out one of our newest videos right  here plus even more looper videos about  the mandalorian  are coming soon subscribe to our youtube  channel and hit the bell so you don't  miss a single one

